// Title: Suspicious Uninstall of Windows Defender Feature via PowerShell
// ID: c443012c-7928-43bf-ac20-7eda5efe61ad
// Status: experimental
// Level: high
// Author: yxinmiracle
// Date: 2025-08-22
// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
// Description: Detects the use of PowerShell with Uninstall-WindowsFeature or Remove-WindowsFeature cmdlets to disable or remove the Windows Defender GUI feature, a common technique used by adversaries to evade defenses.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((process.command_line like "*_Windows-Defender*") and ((process.command_line like "*_Uninstall-WindowsFeature*" or process.command_line like "*_Remove-WindowsFeature*")) and (((process.executable endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\powershell.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\pwsh.exe")) or ((process.pe.original_file_name == "PowerShell_ISE.EXE" or process.pe.original_file_name == "PowerShell.EXE" or process.pe.original_file_name == "pwsh.dll"))))
